From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:06:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/aom_film_grain: Check the predicted luma point count

The predicted luma path copies the reference point count before indexing
res[14] and y_points[14]. The first reference set is checked when
parsed, but gcc 15.2 with -march=x86-64-v3 does not retain that bound
here and reports a stringop-overflow warning.

Check the copied count before both loops, using the existing error path.
This makes the upper bound local and protects the arrays against an
oversized reference count without changing valid streams.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c b/libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c
index bb60c5577418131a5a8c1bf2e23997f0f18025cc..9b836be275552cc2980b83a7ab7f330abd59ceae 100644
--- a/libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c
+++ b/libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c
@@ -225,6 +225,8 @@ int ff_aom_parse_film_grain_sets(AVFilmGrainAFGS1Params *s,
             if (bits_res) {
                 int res[14], pred, granularity;
                 aom->num_y_points = ref->codec.aom.num_y_points;
+                if (aom->num_y_points > 14)
+                    goto error;
                 for (i = 0; i < aom->num_y_points; i++)
                     res[i] = get_bits(gb, bits_res);
                 granularity = get_bits(gb, 3);
